# Edge-border diagnostic run, product default D (ADR-0018 U-1) on the 2x display -- the first live
# reading for the About-window offset survey (docs upgrade-gate/2026-09-10-about-offset-offline-survey.md
# §6.1 C; ADR-0018 §5.1 item 2 / 14:27 "both lanes"). Same shape as smoke-2x-D.env with the diagnostic
# knob on: EDGE_PROFILE=1 becomes WINDOW_SMOKE_EDGE_PROFILE=1 in the child, and window-smoke prints one
# `[edge] …` line per content window after its first frame and again before finish (measurement only,
# nothing asserts on it). MOVE stays on so the same run also yields the move-echo border reading.
# Pre-registration: the record that consumes this run writes the allowed/forbidden columns BEFORE it
# runs (the draft travels with lane O-A's report). Run with:
#   Scripts/lab/run-scenario.sh checkpoint 2x-D-edge <dated batch>     # or: run-scenario.sh smoke 2x-D-edge
TAG=2xD-edge
BATCH=w3-edge-profile
DISPLAY_LOOKS_LIKE=1280x720
ADVERTISED_SCALE=D
MOVE=1
MAXIMIZE=0
TRAY=0
TRAY_CLICK=0
EDGE_PROFILE=1
EXTRA_APPS=notepad
MOVE_TARGET='Notepad|记事本'
REQUIRE_SYMBOL=WINDOW_SMOKE_EDGE_PROFILE
